      "role": "user",
      "content": "i was walking past the main server rack in the office today and the wifi signal was like... pulsing. i could actually hear it. it wasn't just white noise, it was like this rapid, syncopated rhythm. like a drum beat but way faster. \n\ni tried to tap out the pattern on my phone to record it but it's hard to catch the exact tempo. it felt like a sequence of maybe 8-12 distinct pulses before it shifted into a higher frequency stutter. do you think that could actually be a specific data handshake or a packet burst? i can try to describe the intervals more precisely if you can help me decode what the rhythm might mean.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
